  "verdict": "Adding docking / RMT-RTE does NOT improve model confidence, and this holds beyond the HGB analogue. (1) As features on HGB: the 217 RDKit-2D descriptors saturate \u2014 Brier/ECE/AUC are flat-to-worse on random and scaffold (structure is the best rung in both), and +rmt_rte_rec worsens Brier (p=0.037). (2) As the p_QSAR x p_RMT-RTE veto: the precision@0.7 / FPR gains are a thresholding artifact \u2014 coverage collapses (0.45->0.18 random), ranking degrades (AUC 0.918->0.901), and at matched coverage structure alone is more precise (0.987 vs 0.952); mean-fusion is no better and the scaffold split repeats it. (3) On the DMPNN and the DMPNN+HGB STACK: the team's paired k-fold CV (dmpnn_stack_rmt_kfold) shows rmt_rte_rec LOWERS ROC-AUC & PR-AUC for all three models on both splits (blend 0.931->0.925 random, 0.915->0.911 scaffold) \u2014 the earlier single split_00 blend number (0.9343->0.9415) was a one-split artifact. RMT-reconstructed RTE is even weaker than raw RTE (0.76 vs 0.79 HGB ROC), so it only dilutes the structure model. Net: RMT-RTE improves neither confidence nor discrimination on any model here."
